IMPORT `cp4-nouns`
IMPORT `cp4-pension-index`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 58, subsections (1) to (5) and (9) -- THE SURVIVOR'S PENSION.
--
-- A survivor's pension (paragraph 44(1)(d), piece cp3) is paid to the survivor of a contributor. Section
-- 58 says how much: a flat rate benefit and a share of the contributor's retirement pension, the share
-- depending on whether the survivor is under or over 65 and whether the survivor has a retirement pension
-- of their own (subsection (2) then caps the two together). The contributor's retirement pension is the
-- aggregate of three portions (subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)), each indexed by the Pension Index from
-- the month a listed event occurs. Subsections (6) to (8.1), which cut the pensions down when the survivor
-- also has a disability pension, are in the next module, cp4-survivors-pension-offsets.l4.
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: the Pension Index (s 43), the survivor's own retirement pension
-- portions (s 46), the adjustment under s 45(2), the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average (s 42(1)), the
-- Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings (s 18, piece cp1), the first and second additional monthly
-- pensionable earnings (ss 48.1, 48.2, 51), the retirement pension used for the base portion (s 57(2) in
-- this piece, whose result the caller passes), whether the person is a survivor, a survivor with dependent
-- children or disabled (ss 42, 44; piece cp3), and a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (ss 55,
-- 55.1; piece cp3). All amounts are monthly dollars.

§ `Section 58 (subsections 1 to 5 and 9) -- amount of survivor's pension`

§§ `Section 58(1.1) -- the flat rate benefit`

-- src:1739 | Amount of flat rate benefit
-- src:1740 | (1.1) The amount of the flat rate benefit referred to in subparagraphs (1)(a)(i) and (a.1)(i) is
-- src:1741 | (a) in the year 1986, ninety-one dollars and six cents; or
-- src:1742 | (b) in the year 1987 or any subsequent year, an amount calculated by multiplying
-- src:1743 | (i) the amount of the flat rate benefit that would have been payable for a month in the year preceding that year
-- src:1744 | by
-- src:1745 | (ii) the ratio that the Pension Index for the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable bears to the Pension Index for the year preceding that year.
@ref Act s 58(1.1) (src:1740-1745)
GIVEN `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 58(1.1) — the flat rate benefit of a survivor's pension` `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` MEANS
    -- Unlike subsection 56(2), the year 1987 runs from the 1986 amount here (NOTES.md, finding on the two flat rates).
    BRANCH
        IF `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` EQUALS 1986
            THEN JUST 91.06
        IF `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` AT LEAST 1987
            THEN `cp4 an amount that may be missing times a ratio that may be missing` (`s 58(1.1) — the flat rate benefit of a survivor's pension` (`the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` MINUS 1) `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`) (`cp4 the ratio of the Pension Index for a year to the Pension Index for the year before` `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Section 58(1) -- the basic monthly amount where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor`

-- Not a provision: the number of months by which a person's age at a time is less than 45. Reaching 45 goes
-- through section 2(2): the person is deemed to reach 45 at the start of the month after the birthday month.
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      time IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp4 the months by which a person's age at a time is less than 45` `date of birth` time MEANS
    max 0 (`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` time (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` 45))

-- src:1719 | (a) in the case of a survivor who has not reached 65 years of age and to whom no retirement pension is payable under this Act or a provincial pension plan, for any month before January 2019, a basic monthly amount consisting of
-- src:1720 | (i) a flat rate benefit, calculated as provided in subsection (1.1), and
-- src:1721 | (ii) 37.5% of the amount of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1722 | (A) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3),
-- src:1723 | (B) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3.1), and
-- src:1724 | (C) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3.4),
-- src:1725 | reduced, unless the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children or unless he is disabled, by 1/120 for each month by which the age of the survivor at the time of the death of the contributor is less than forty-five years, and reduced, if at any time after the death of the contributor the survivor ceases to be
-- src:1726 | (iii) a survivor with dependent children and is not at that time disabled, or
-- src:1727 | (iv) disabled and is not at that time a survivor with dependent children,
-- src:1728 | by 1/120 for each month by which the age of the survivor at that time is less than forty-five years;
@ref Act s 58(1)(a) (src:1719-1728)
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor is disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day of the death of the contributor` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the survivor ceased to be a survivor with dependent children while not disabled, or ceased to be disabled while not a survivor with dependent children` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` `the flat rate benefit` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` `the survivor is disabled` `the survivor's date of birth` `the day of the death of the contributor` `the day on which the survivor ceased to be a survivor with dependent children while not disabled, or ceased to be disabled while not a survivor with dependent children` MEANS
    -- NOTHING: the reductions together take more than the whole amount (more than 120 months of 1/120); the text
    -- gives no floor (NOTES.md, fork register).
    IF `the months of reduction` GREATER THAN 120
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the basic amount` TIMES (1 MINUS (`the months of reduction` DIVIDED BY 120)))
    WHERE
        `the basic amount` MEANS
            `the flat rate benefit` PLUS (37.5% TIMES (  `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`
                                                           PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`
                                                           PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`))
        -- "reduced, unless the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent
        -- children or unless he is disabled, by 1/120 for each month by which the age of the survivor at the time of
        -- the death of the contributor is less than forty-five years"
        `the months of reduction at death` MEANS
            IF `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` OR `the survivor is disabled`
            THEN 0
            ELSE `cp4 the months by which a person's age at a time is less than 45` `the survivor's date of birth` `the day of the death of the contributor`
        -- "and reduced, if at any time after the death of the contributor the survivor ceases to be (iii) ... or (iv) ...,
        -- by 1/120 for each month by which the age of the survivor at that time is less than forty-five years"
        `the months of reduction on ceasing` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the survivor ceased to be a survivor with dependent children while not disabled, or ceased to be disabled while not a survivor with dependent children`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
            WHEN JUST ceased THEN `cp4 the months by which a person's age at a time is less than 45` `the survivor's date of birth` ceased
        `the months of reduction` MEANS `the months of reduction at death` PLUS `the months of reduction on ceasing`

-- src:1729 | (a.1) in the case of a survivor who has not reached 65 years of age and to whom no retirement pension is payable under this Act or a provincial pension plan, for any month after December 2018, a basic monthly amount consisting of
