    -- No reduction by 1/120 appears in paragraph (a.1).
    `the flat rate benefit` PLUS (37.5% TIMES (  `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`
                                                   PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`
                                                   PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`))

-- src:1735 | (b) in the case of a survivor who has reached 65 years of age and to whom no retirement pension is payable under this Act or a provincial pension plan, a basic monthly amount equal to 60% of the amount of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1736 | (i) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3),
-- src:1737 | (ii) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3.1), and
-- src:1738 | (iii) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3.4).
@ref Act s 58(1)(b) (src:1735-1738)
GIVEN `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(1)(b) — the survivor's pension where the survivor has reached 65 and no retirement pension is payable` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` MEANS
    60% TIMES (  `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`
              PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`
              PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`)

-- src:1718 | 58 (1) Subject to this section, a survivor’s pension payable to the survivor of a contributor is a basic monthly amount as follows:
@ref Act s 58(1) (src:1718)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the survivor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `a retirement pension is payable to the survivor under this Act or a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor is disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the death of the contributor` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the survivor ceased to be a survivor with dependent children while not disabled, or ceased to be disabled while not a survivor with dependent children` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 58(1) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor` month `the survivor's date of birth` `a retirement pension is payable to the survivor under this Act or a provincial pension plan` `the flat rate benefit` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` `the survivor is disabled` `the day of the death of the contributor` `the day on which the survivor ceased to be a survivor with dependent children while not disabled, or ceased to be disabled while not a survivor with dependent children` MEANS
    -- NOTHING where a retirement pension is payable to the survivor: subsection (2) governs that case.
    BRANCH
        IF `a retirement pension is payable to the survivor under this Act or a provincial pension plan`
            THEN NOTHING
        IF `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the survivor's date of birth` 65 (`the month of a date` month)
            THEN JUST (`s 58(1)(b) — the survivor's pension where the survivor has reached 65 and no retirement pension is payable` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`)
        IF month LESS THAN (YMD 2019 1 1)
            THEN `s 58(1)(a) — the survivor's pension for a month before 2019 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` `the flat rate benefit` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` `the survivor is disabled` `the survivor's date of birth` `the day of the death of the contributor` `the day on which the survivor ceased to be a survivor with dependent children while not disabled, or ceased to be disabled while not a survivor with dependent children`
        OTHERWISE JUST (`s 58(1)(a.1) — the survivor's pension for a month after 2018 where the survivor is under 65 and no retirement pension is payable` `the flat rate benefit` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`)

§§ `Section 58(3) to (3.6) -- the three portions of the contributor's retirement pension`

-- Not a provision: an amount multiplied by the Pension Index ratio "for the purpose of calculating the monthly
-- amount of the survivor's pension for months commencing with the month in which" an event occurred. A month is
-- multiplied when it is the month of the first event or later; with no event, it is not multiplied.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      month IS A DATE
      `the months in which one of the events described in paragraphs (3)(a) to (e) occurred` IS A LIST OF DATE
      ratio IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp4 an amount multiplied by the Pension Index ratio for months from the first event` amount month `the months in which one of the events described in paragraphs (3)(a) to (e) occurred` ratio MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN event YIELD `the month of a date` event AT MOST `the month of a date` month) `the months in which one of the events described in paragraphs (3)(a) to (e) occurred`
    THEN amount TIMES ratio
    ELSE amount

-- src:1813 | (3) The amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension that is to be used for the purposes of subsections (1) and (2) is an amount calculated as provided in paragraph 57(2)(a), (b) or (c), multiplied, for the purpose of calculating the monthly amount of the survivor’s pension for months commencing with the month in which
-- src:1814 | (a) a survivor’s pension became payable to the survivor by reason of a disability that began after the death of the contributor,
-- src:1815 | (b) the survivor reached sixty-five years of age, not having reached that age at the time of the death of the contributor,
-- src:1816 | (c) the survivor’s pension under this Act or the survivor’s retirement pension under this Act or a provincial pension plan commenced to be payable, whichever is the later,
-- src:1817 | (d) a survivor’s pension became payable to the survivor under this Act in circumstances other than those described in paragraph (a), (b) or (c), or
-- src:1818 | (e) the survivor has had an adjustment to the survivor’s retirement pension pursuant to subsection 55(7) or 55.2(9) following a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings,
-- src:1819 | by the ratio that the Pension Index for the year that includes that month bears to the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died.
@ref Act s 58(3) (src:1813-1819)
GIVEN `the amount calculated as provided in paragraph 57(2)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A NUMBER
      month IS A DATE
      `the months in which one of the events described in paragraphs (a) to (e) occurred` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the ratio that the Pension Index for the year that includes that month bears to the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` `the amount calculated as provided in paragraph 57(2)(a), (b) or (c)` month `the months in which one of the events described in paragraphs (a) to (e) occurred` `the ratio that the Pension Index for the year that includes that month bears to the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died` MEANS
    `cp4 an amount multiplied by the Pension Index ratio for months from the first event` `the amount calculated as provided in paragraph 57(2)(a), (b) or (c)` month `the months in which one of the events described in paragraphs (a) to (e) occurred` `the ratio that the Pension Index for the year that includes that month bears to the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died`

