-- src:1846 | Pension Index limitation removed
-- src:1847 | (4) For the purpose of calculating the monthly amount of a survivor’s pension under subsection (3) in a case where the survivor’s pension commences with a month in a year after 1973 and is in respect of a contributor who died prior to 1974, the ratio referred to in that subsection shall be calculated as if the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died had not been subject to the limitation referred to in paragraph 43.1(2)(a) of the Canada Pension Plan, chapter C-5 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, of 1.02 times the Pension Index for the preceding year.
@ref Act s 58(4) (src:1847)
GIVEN `the year in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
      `the year in which the survivor's pension commences` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died, calculated as if it had not been subject to the limitation of 1.02 times the Pension Index for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(4) — the Pension Index for the year of the contributor's death that the ratio of subsection (3) uses` `the year in which the contributor died` `the year in which the survivor's pension commences` `the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died` `the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died, calculated as if it had not been subject to the limitation of 1.02 times the Pension Index for the preceding year` MEANS
    -- The limitation is that of paragraph 43.1(2)(a) of the Canada Pension Plan, chapter C-5 of the Revised
    -- Statutes of Canada, 1970; that Act is not among the texts read, so both indices are supplied.
    IF (`the year in which the contributor died` LESS THAN 1974) AND (`the year in which the survivor's pension commences` GREATER THAN 1973)
    THEN `the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died, calculated as if it had not been subject to the limitation of 1.02 times the Pension Index for the preceding year`
    ELSE `the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died`

-- src:1848 | Calculation of amount of retirement pension to survivor
-- src:1849 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2), the monthly amount of the retirement pension payable to the survivor of a contributor shall be calculated without regard to any provision of the provincial pension plan referred to in that subsection that reduces the pensions of contributors who have reached sixty-five years of age or precludes the payment of pensions to those contributors by reason of their employment earnings.
@ref Act s 58(5) (src:1849)
GIVEN `the monthly amount of the retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount by which a provision of that plan reduces, or precludes payment of, the pension of a contributor who has reached sixty-five years of age by reason of employment earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(5) — the monthly amount of the survivor's retirement pension to use in subsection (2)` `the monthly amount of the retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan` `the amount by which a provision of that plan reduces, or precludes payment of, the pension of a contributor who has reached sixty-five years of age by reason of employment earnings` MEANS
    -- "calculated without regard to any provision of the provincial pension plan ... that reduces the pensions of
    -- contributors who have reached sixty-five years of age or precludes the payment of pensions ... by reason of
    -- their employment earnings": what such a provision took away is put back.
    `the monthly amount of the retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan` PLUS `the amount by which a provision of that plan reduces, or precludes payment of, the pension of a contributor who has reached sixty-five years of age by reason of employment earnings`

§§ `Section 58(2) -- where a survivor's pension and a retirement pension are both payable`

-- Not a provision: "an amount that, when added to X, is equal to the amount of a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of Y,
-- adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2)": the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, once adjusted. The
-- adjustment under 45(2) (piece cp3) is a ratio of Pension Indexes, supplied; 1 where nothing is adjusted.
GIVEN average IS A NUMBER
      `the adjustment under subsection 45(2), as a ratio` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp4 a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, adjusted` average `the adjustment under subsection 45(2), as a ratio` MEANS
    ((25% TIMES average) DIVIDED BY 12) TIMES `the adjustment under subsection 45(2), as a ratio`

-- Not a provision: A minus B, where B is the lesser of 40% of A and 40% of the survivor's own portion
-- (the formulas "C - D" and "A - B" of subsection (2)).
GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
      `the survivor's own portion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp4 a share less the lesser of 40% of it and 40% of the survivor's own portion` share `the survivor's own portion` MEANS
    share MINUS (min (40% TIMES share) (40% TIMES `the survivor's own portion`))

-- src:1748 | (a) in the case of a survivor who has not reached sixty-five years of age and whose retirement pension commences to be payable after December 31, 1997, the aggregate of
-- src:1749 | (i) the aggregate of
-- src:1750 | (A) a flat rate benefit, calculated as provided in subsection (1.1), or, if a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the survivor, the greater of
-- src:1751 | (I) the flat rate benefit, and
-- src:1752 | (II) the post-retirement disability benefit, and
-- src:1753 | (B) the lesser of
-- src:1754 | (I) the amount determined by the formula
-- src:1755 | C – D
-- src:1756 | where
-- src:1757 | C is 37.5% of the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in subsection (3), and
-- src:1758 | D is the lesser of
-- src:1759 | (1) 40% of C, and
-- src:1760 | (2) 40% of the amount of the portion of the survivor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(a), without regard to subsections 46(3) to (6), and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2), and
-- src:1761 | (II) an amount that, when added to the amount of the portion of the survivor’s retirement pension that is calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(a), without regard to subsections 46(3) to (6), and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2), is equal to the amount of a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s retirement pension commenced to be payable, adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2) as if the benefit had commenced to be payable in the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s retirement pension commenced to be payable,
-- src:1762 | (ii) the amount determined by the formula
-- src:1763 | C – D
-- src:1764 | where
-- src:1765 | C is 37.5% of the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in subsection (3.1), and
-- src:1766 | D is the lesser of
-- src:1767 | (1) 40% of C, and
-- src:1768 | (2) 40% of the amount of the portion of the survivor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(b), without regard to subsections 46(3.1) to (6), and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2), and
-- src:1769 | (iii) the amount determined by the formula
-- src:1770 | C – D
-- src:1771 | where
-- src:1772 | C is 37.5% of the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in subsection (3.4), and
-- src:1773 | D is the lesser of
-- src:1774 | (1) 40% of C, and
-- src:1775 | (2) 40% of the amount of the portion of the survivor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(c), without regard to subsections 46(3.1) to (6) and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2);
@ref Act s 58(2)(a) (src:1748-1775)
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the survivor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the post-retirement disability benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(2)(a) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` `the flat rate benefit` `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the survivor` `the post-retirement disability benefit` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` MEANS
    -- (i): (A) the flat rate benefit, or the greater of it and a post-retirement disability benefit, plus (B) the
    -- lesser of (I) C - D and (II) the top-up to the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average.
    -- (ii) and (iii): C - D for the first and the second additional portions.
    (`the flat rate benefit or the greater of it and the post-retirement disability benefit` PLUS `the lesser of (I) and (II)`)
        PLUS (`cp4 a share less the lesser of 40% of it and 40% of the survivor's own portion` (37.5% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`) (`the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`))
        PLUS (`cp4 a share less the lesser of 40% of it and 40% of the survivor's own portion` (37.5% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`) (`the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`))
    WHERE
        `the flat rate benefit or the greater of it and the post-retirement disability benefit` MEANS
            IF `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the survivor`
            THEN max `the flat rate benefit` `the post-retirement disability benefit`
            ELSE `the flat rate benefit`
        `the lesser of (I) and (II)` MEANS
            min (`cp4 a share less the lesser of 40% of it and 40% of the survivor's own portion` (37.5% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`) (`the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`))
                (`the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` MINUS `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`)

-- src:1776 | (b) in the case of a survivor who has not reached sixty-five years of age and whose retirement pension commences to be payable before January 1, 1998, the aggregate of
-- src:1777 | (i) a flat rate benefit, calculated as provided in subsection (1.1), and
-- src:1778 | (ii) the lesser of
-- src:1779 | (A) 37.5% of the amount of the contributor’s retirement pension, calculated as provided in subsection (3), and
-- src:1780 | (B) an amount that, when added to the survivor’s retirement pension (calculated without regard to subsections 46(3) to (6) but in accordance with subsection 45(2)), is equal to the amount of a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s retirement pension commenced to be payable, and for each of the two preceding years, adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2) as if the benefit had commenced to be payable in the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s retirement pension commenced to be payable; or
@ref Act s 58(2)(b) (src:1776-1780)
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(2)(b) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences before 1998` `the flat rate benefit` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` MEANS
    -- Before 1998 a retirement pension had no additional portion, so the survivor's retirement pension is the base portion.
    `the flat rate benefit` PLUS (min (37.5% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`) (`the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` MINUS `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`))

-- src:1781 | (c) in the case of a survivor who has reached 65 years of age and who was born after December 31, 1932 and whose retirement pension commences to be payable after December 31, 1997, the aggregate of
-- src:1782 | (i) the lesser of
-- src:1783 | (A) the amount determined by the formula
-- src:1784 | A – B
-- src:1785 | where
-- src:1786 | A is 60% of the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in subsection (3), and
-- src:1787 | B is the lesser of
