-- src:1789 | (II) 40% of the amount of the portion of the survivor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(a), without regard to subsections 46(3) to (6), and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2), and
-- src:1790 | (B) an amount that, when added to the amount of the portion of the survivor’s retirement pension that is calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(a), without regard to subsections 46(3) to (6), and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2), is equal to the amount of a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s retirement pension commenced to be payable, adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2) as if the benefit had commenced to be payable in the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s retirement pension commenced to be payable,
-- src:1791 | (ii) the amount determined by the formula
-- src:1792 | A – B
-- src:1793 | where
-- src:1794 | A is 60% of the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in subsection (3.1), and
-- src:1795 | B is the lesser of
-- src:1796 | (I) 40% of A, and
-- src:1797 | (II) 40% of the amount of the portion of the survivor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(b), without regard to subsections 46(3.1) to (6), and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2), and
-- src:1798 | (iii) the amount determined by the formula
-- src:1799 | A – B
-- src:1800 | where
-- src:1801 | A is 60% of the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in subsection (3.4), and
-- src:1802 | B is the lesser of
-- src:1803 | (I) 40% of A, and
-- src:1804 | (II) 40% of the amount of the portion of the survivor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(c), without regard to subsections 46(3.1) to (6), and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2);
-- src:1805 | or
@ref Act s 58(2)(c) (src:1781-1805)
GIVEN `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(2)(c) — the survivor's pension where the survivor has reached 65, was born after 1932 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` MEANS
    (min (`cp4 a share less the lesser of 40% of it and 40% of the survivor's own portion` (60% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`) (`the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`))
         (`the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` MINUS `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`))
        PLUS (`cp4 a share less the lesser of 40% of it and 40% of the survivor's own portion` (60% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`) (`the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`))
        PLUS (`cp4 a share less the lesser of 40% of it and 40% of the survivor's own portion` (60% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`) (`the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`))

-- src:1806 | (d) in any other case, the aggregate of
-- src:1807 | (i) the lesser of
-- src:1808 | (A) 60% of the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in subsection (3), and
-- src:1809 | (B) an amount that, when added to the amount of the portion of the survivor’s retirement pension that is calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(a), without regard to subsections 46(3) to (6), and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2), is equal to the amount of a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s retirement pension commenced to be payable, and for each of the two preceding years, adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2) as if the benefit had commenced to be payable in the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s retirement pension commenced to be payable,
-- src:1810 | (ii) 60% of the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in subsection (3.1), and
-- src:1811 | (iii) 60% of the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as provided in subsection (3.4).
@ref Act s 58(2)(d) (src:1806-1811)
GIVEN `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(2)(d) — the survivor's pension in any other case where a retirement pension is also payable` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` MEANS
    (min (60% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`) (`the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` MINUS `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`))
        PLUS (60% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`)
        PLUS (60% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`)

-- src:1747 | (2) Where a survivor’s pension under this Act and a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan are payable to the survivor of a contributor, the basic monthly amount of the survivor’s pension payable to the survivor is
@ref Act s 58(2) (src:1747)
GIVEN `a survivor's pension under this Act and a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan are payable to the survivor` IS A BOOLEAN
      month IS A DATE
      `the survivor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the survivor's retirement pension commences to be payable` IS A DATE
      `the flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the survivor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the post-retirement disability benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` `a survivor's pension under this Act and a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan are payable to the survivor` month `the survivor's date of birth` `the day on which the survivor's retirement pension commences to be payable` `the flat rate benefit` `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the survivor` `the post-retirement disability benefit` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` MEANS
    -- NOTHING where subsection (2) does not apply (not both pensions payable): subsection (1) governs.
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a survivor's pension under this Act and a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan are payable to the survivor`
            THEN NOTHING
        IF (NOT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the survivor's date of birth` 65 (`the month of a date` month)) AND (`the day on which the survivor's retirement pension commences to be payable` AT LEAST (YMD 1998 1 1))
            THEN JUST (`s 58(2)(a) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` `the flat rate benefit` `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the survivor` `the post-retirement disability benefit` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted`)
        IF NOT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the survivor's date of birth` 65 (`the month of a date` month)
            THEN JUST (`s 58(2)(b) — the survivor's pension where the survivor is under 65 and the retirement pension commences before 1998` `the flat rate benefit` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted`)
        IF (`the survivor's date of birth` AT LEAST (YMD 1933 1 1)) AND (`the day on which the survivor's retirement pension commences to be payable` AT LEAST (YMD 1998 1 1))
            THEN JUST (`s 58(2)(c) — the survivor's pension where the survivor has reached 65, was born after 1932 and the retirement pension commences after 1997` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted`)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`s 58(2)(d) — the survivor's pension in any other case where a retirement pension is also payable` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections (3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the survivor's own retirement pension portions under paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted`)

§§ `Section 58(9) -- when a survivor first becomes qualified`

-- src:1921 | Interpretation
-- src:1922 | (9) For the purposes of this section, a survivor first becomes qualified to receive a survivor’s pension in the month following the month in which the survivor first met the criteria of subsection 44(1) in relation to that pension.
@ref Act s 58(9) (src:1922)
GIVEN `the month in which the survivor first met the criteria of subsection 44(1) in relation to that pension` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 58(9) — the month in which the survivor first becomes qualified to receive the survivor's pension` `the month in which the survivor first met the criteria of subsection 44(1) in relation to that pension` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` `the month in which the survivor first met the criteria of subsection 44(1) in relation to that pension`
